# Project Conventions

## Source of truth
- Requirements: docs/00-brief.md
- Architecture: docs/01-architecture.md
- AI prompts: docs/02-prompts.md
- Decisions: docs/03-decisions.md

## Hard constraints
- TypeScript strict mode. No `any`. No `unknown` without narrowing.
- Zod schemas at ALL data boundaries (forms, file parsing, AI outputs).
- Convex is the single source of truth for operational state.
- Invite lifecycle transitions enforced server-side in mutations (never free-form status writes).
- Progress is always computed from queries, never stored as derived counters.
- AI-extracted data is NEVER written to DB without human confirmation.
- No SSR. Static site generation only.
- Biome for formatting and linting. No eslint/prettier.
- Never commit .env, node_modules, or .DS_Store.

## Patterns
- Shared types between frontend and Convex via Zod schemas that mirror Convex validators.
- Small, focused components. Meaningful names. No god components.
- Prefer Convex reactive queries (useQuery) for live data. No polling.
- Server-shaped queries: Convex queries return screen-ready view models (joins + computed fields). UI renders, not orchestrates.
- Typed errors on mutations with known failure modes (sendInvite, resendInvite, AI import): return `{ ok: false, code, message }` for expected failures. Throw only for unexpected/invariant failures.
- Storybook: shared components must have stories for loading/empty/error + all status variants, not just happy path.
- Mock auth via role switcher (Vend Admin / Tenant Admin), not real auth.
- Tenant admin is a separate entity (tenantAdmins table), not inlined on tenants.
- Access codes are unique per member and stable across resends unless explicitly regenerated.
- Commits: conventional commits (feat/fix/chore/docs), small and PR-sized.

## Scope
- Do NOT invent features beyond docs/00-brief.md.
- If ambiguous, add a TODO comment and note in docs/03-decisions.md.

